      "text": "## 1. RESPIRATORY: β2-Agonists"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#007",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMECHANISM:\n  β2-receptor (Gs-coupled GPCR) → adenylyl cyclase → cAMP ↑ → PKA activation\n  PKA phosphorylates: myosin light chain kinase (MLCK) → inactivation → smooth muscle relaxation\n  Also: mast cell stabilization; mucociliary clearance ↑\n  Selectivity: β2 >> β1 (cardiac); at high doses → β1 effects (tachycardia)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#008",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SABA — SHORT-ACTING β2-AGONISTS (rescue):\n  Salbutamol (albuterol): onset 5 min; duration 4-6 hrs; racemic (R-isomer active)\n  Terbutaline: similar; also used for premature labor (tocolytic)\n  Indication: acute bronchospasm (asthma/COPD exacerbation); exercise-induced bronchoconstriction (EIB)\n  Adverse: tachycardia, tremor, HYPOKALEMIA (K+ shifted intracellularly by cAMP); dysrhythmia at high doses\n  Monitoring: K+ in high-dose nebulization (e.g., status asthmaticus)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#009",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LABA — LONG-ACTING β2-AGONISTS (maintenance):\n  Salmeterol: onset 30 min; duration 12 hrs; lipophilic → anchors in membrane → slow release\n  Formoterol: onset 5 min (faster than salmeterol); duration 12 hrs; can be used as rescue in some regimens\n  Indacaterol: once-daily; 24-hr duration; for COPD\n  CRITICAL: LABA monotherapy is CONTRAINDICATED in asthma (SMART trial: increased asthma mortality)\n    Always combine with ICS in asthma (LABA+ICS fixed-dose inhaler)\n    Rationale: ICS treats underlying inflammation; LABA controls symptoms; LABA alone masks worsening\n  In COPD: LABA monotherapy acceptable (no ICS mandate); LABA+LAMA = standard dual bronchodilator"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#010",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MECHANISM OF TOLERANCE:\n  β-receptor downregulation with chronic SABA overuse → reduced rescue effect\n  Clinical significance: overuse of SABA (>2 canisters/month) = marker of poor control\n```"
    },
