      "text": "## 2. RESPIRATORY: Anticholinergics (SAMA/LAMA)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#013",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMECHANISM:\n  Muscarinic M3 receptors: activation → Gq → IP3/DAG → smooth muscle contraction + mucus secretion\n  Anticholinergics block M3 → reduce bronchoconstriction and mucus hypersecretion\n  β2-agonists more potent bronchodilators acutely; anticholinergics better for mucus/COPD\n  Synergy: LABA+LAMA combination more effective than either alone (different mechanisms)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#014",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SAMA — SHORT-ACTING MUSCARINIC ANTAGONIST:\n  Ipratropium: onset 15-30 min; duration 6-8 hrs; quaternary ammonium → poor GI absorption → few systemic effects\n  Indicated: COPD first-line; acute asthma when inadequate β2 response (add-on)\n  Combination: salbutamol + ipratropium (Duovent/Combivent) — synergistic in acute COPD exacerbation"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#015",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LAMA — LONG-ACTING MUSCARINIC ANTAGONIST:\n  Tiotropium (Spiriva): once-daily; kinetic selectivity M1/M3 over M2 (M2 presynaptic → inhibits ACh release; blocking M2 would paradoxically increase ACh)\n    Dissociation rate: very slow from M1/M3 but fast from M2 → effective selectivity\n  Umeclidinium, aclidinium, glycopyrronium: once-daily alternatives; similar profile\n  Adverse: urinary retention (M3 in detrusor), constipation, dry mouth, blurred vision (angle-closure glaucoma risk)\n  Contraindication: narrow-angle glaucoma (use with caution; ensure not acute)\n  Clinical: tiotropium reduces COPD exacerbation rate, hospitalizations; slows FEV1 decline"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#016",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GINA / GOLD STEP-UP:\n  Asthma: ICS → ICS+LABA → ICS+LABA+LAMA (add tiotropium at Step 4-5)\n  COPD: LAMA or LABA monotherapy → LAMA+LABA → LAMA+LABA+ICS (if eosinophils/FEV1 <50%)\n```"
    },
    {
