      "text": "## 3. RESPIRATORY: Inhaled Corticosteroids (ICS)"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#019",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMECHANISM:\n  GCS (glucocorticoid receptor) → nuclear translocation → transcription factor modulation:\n    Transactivation: anti-inflammatory genes (IL-10, annexin-1)\n    Transrepression: inhibit NF-κB → ↓ IL-4, IL-5, IL-13, eotaxin, TNF-α\n  Results: reduced eosinophil infiltration, mast cell degranulation, mucus production, edema\n  Inhaled delivery: local lung effect; minimizes systemic exposure vs oral steroids"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#020",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "AGENTS:\n  Fluticasone propionate (FP): high potency; high first-pass effect → low oral bioavailability\n  Budesonide: moderate; swallowed fraction inactivated by hepatic first-pass; used in nebulized form (croup)\n  Beclomethasone (BDP): prodrug → active beclomethasone-17-monopropionate in lungs\n  Mometasone: high receptor affinity; once-daily; intranasal + inhaled\n  Ciclesonide: prodrug activated in airways; lower oropharyngeal deposition"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#021",
      "path": [
        "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:medicine:08-respiratory-gi, git-history:medicine:08-respiratory-gi]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "current_path": "medicine/08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:respiratory-gi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[respiratory, gi]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ADVERSE EFFECTS:\n  Local: oropharyngeal candidiasis (preventable with spacer + rinse/gargle after use)\n  Local: dysphonia (hoarseness) — muscle effect on vocal cords; often reversible\n  Systemic (high-dose chronic): HPA suppression (rare at standard doses; significant at fluticasone >1000 mcg/day)\n  Systemic: reduced bone density (long-term high-dose); fracture risk; monitor DEXA\n  Pediatric growth: some reduction at high doses; outweighed by asthma control benefit\n  Not the same as systemic corticosteroids: much lower systemic exposure at therapeutic doses"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-RESPIRATORY-GI.md#022",
      "path": [
