        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "08 - Respiratory and GI Drugs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMETHYLXANTHINES:\n  Theophylline: narrow therapeutic index (TI); PDE (phosphodiesterase) inhibitor → cAMP ↑\n    Also: adenosine receptor antagonist (central stimulant); anti-inflammatory at low concentrations\n  Mechanism: non-selective PDE inhibitor; weak bronchodilator; histone deacetylase activation (anti-inflam)\n  Pharmacokinetics: oral; hepatic CYP1A2 + CYP3A4 metabolism; many drug interactions\n    Inducers: smoking, rifampicin, carbamazepine → lower levels → inadequate effect\n    Inhibitors: ciprofloxacin, erythromycin, cimetidine → elevated levels → toxicity\n  Therapeutic range: 5-15 mg/L; toxicity: 20+ mg/L (seizures, arrhythmias, nausea, vomiting)\n  Monitoring: serum levels; ECG; status of interacting drugs\n  Role: largely replaced by safer LABA/ICS combinations; still used in LMIC and some COPD"
    }
